      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters, so `café` becomes `cafe`. All 4 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass, including 2 new ones.\n\nThe bug was in `slug/core.py`: any non-ASCII letter fell into the `isalpha()` branch and was dropped. The fix decomposes the string with NFKD and drops the combining accent marks, so `é` becomes `e`, `Crème Brûlée` becomes `creme-brulee`, and `ü` becomes `u`.\n\nA few letters don't decompose into a base letter, so I added a small map for them: `ß`→`ss`, `æ`→`ae`, `œ`→`oe`, `ø`→`o`, `ł`→`l`, `đ`→`d`, `ð`→`d`, `þ`→`th`. Without it, `Straße` would still lose its `ß`. Any other letter with no mapping is still dropped, as before. The map is my choice, so trim it if you'd rather keep the change minimal.\n\nI also added a regression test in `tests/test_core.py` covering both cases. I haven't committed anything.",
